    "result_text": "Done. The build succeeds with all tests green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it passes).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change implements the welcome-notification requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added a `NOTIFY` logger** alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n   ```\n\n2. **Emitted the welcome notification on successful create** by adding an `enqueueWelcomeNotification(owner)` call in `createOwner(...)` \u2014 placed after the owner is persisted (so it has its generated `id` and derived `memberId`) and only reached on success (any rejecting rule throws before this point):\n   ```java\n   private void enqueueWelcomeNotification(Owner owner) {\n       NOTIFY.info(\"Welcome notification queued: id={} memberId={}\",\n           owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   }\n   ```\n\nThe emitted line carries both the owner id and the memberId, satisfying the test's `AuditLogCapture(\"NOTIFY\")` assertion that a NOTIFY line contains both `String.valueOf(id)` and the `memberId` read back from `GET /api/owners/{id}`. This follows the existing pattern in the file (the parallel `AUDIT` logger usage), matching the surrounding style and comment density.",
